/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hogoww/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hogoww/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hogoww/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hogoww/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hogoww/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I tried to keep it short, might be too short ^^\"\r\nHow about that ?\r\n\r\nWhen capturing the mouse in an event handler while handling a mouse event, the mouse event propagation will stop and no subsequent event handler will be trigger for this mouse event. \r\nIf you want the mouse event to keep propagating, make use of [method Object.call_deferred] to capture the mouse after all event handler have been executed.\r\n\r\nThis version seems to be overlong, but at least it seems more complete to enable discution of what it should be.","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:00:17Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T15:00:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123336#discussion_r3969903866","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123336","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3969903866"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123336#discussion_r3969903866"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123336"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3969903866/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":927,"original_line":927,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3969818123,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3969938704","pull_request_review_id":515