":"https://api.github.com/users/hogoww/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hogoww/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hogoww/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hogoww/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Cool, I wasn't sure I was clear enough ^^\r\n\r\n> it isn't as clear or friendly for C# users where the access is different\r\n\r\nDo I have to consider C# and update its documentation as well to keep them in sync if possible ? I'm not familiar with the C# version.\r\n\r\nHow about:\r\nIf you're setting the mouse_mode to MOUSE_MODE_CAPTURED while handling a mouse event, the mouse event will stop propagating to the next event handlers.\r\nIf you want the mouse event to keep propagating, you should defer the set_mouse_mode call with [method Object.call_deferred] to capture the mouse *after* all event handler have been executed.\r\n\r\nHow much space would be reasonable to take for such a note ?\r\nFor instance, would it be okay to explicitly give the code example ```Input.call_deferred(&\"set_mouse_mode\",Input.MOUSE_MODE_CAPTURED)```","created_at":"2026-09-09T19:35:36Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T19:35:36Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123336#discussion_r3972283382","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123336","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3972283382"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123336#discussion_r3972283382"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123336"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3972283382/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":927,"original_line":927,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":